abstract: >-
  AetherMemory is the twelfth candidate of the Aether family. It investigates
  whether persistent knowledge in autonomous multi-agent systems requires a
  distinct architectural dimension — a memory lifecycle — that cannot be
  reduced to storage (AetherGit), consistency (AetherMesh), policy
  (AetherPolicy), or audit (AetherAudit). Current status: Phase 0
  (Architectural Hypothesis). Decision: (E) Undetermined (interim). No
  implementation exists. The repository contains the hypothesis, the boundary
  map, the falsification plan, partial execution of M-F1, M-F2, and M-F3, a
  status declaration for M-F4, the independence decision, and an independent
  review by Jonathan Rabe (2026-11-19). AetherMemory is a candidate, not a
  result.
date-released: 2026-11-20
